<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia says no specifics in Thai sugar talks.</title>
<headline>Australia says no specifics in Thai sugar talks.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian and Thailand sugar industries had had initial dialogue on the benefit of future discussions on matters of mutual interest, a spokeswoman for Queensland Sugar Corp (QSC) told Reuters.</p>
<p>However, nothing specific had been discussed so far, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Thai Cane and Sugar Board secretary general Pramote Vidtayasuk said on Monday that the Thai Cane and Sugar Board and the Queensland Sugar Corp were set to cooperate to seek a reduction in import tariffs imposed on sugar exports to Japan and South Korea.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
